===============================================================================
ETHICAL USE, RESEARCH, AND TESTING COVENANT
===============================================================================

1. SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH & TESTING PURPOSE:
   The Software is provided primarily as an open experimental cryptographic
   primitive for academic research, peer review, benchmarking, security
   auditing, formal verification, and ethical cryptanalysis. Users are
   explicitly authorized and encouraged to test, stress-test, fuzz, simulate,
   and attempt to break or analyze the construction for scientific evaluation.

2. ETHICAL AND DEFENSIVE APPLICATION:
   The Software shall be used exclusively for lawful, defensive, academic,
   educational, and ethical purposes. The Software must NOT be used:
   a) To design, develop, support, or distribute malicious software, ransomware,
      trojans, spyware, or cyber weapons;
   b) In unauthorized attacks, illegal penetration, or unlicensed surveillance
      against third-party computer systems or networks;
   c) To violate any applicable international, national, or local privacy,
      cybersecurity, or human rights laws.

3. RESPONSIBLE DISCLOSURE:
   Any cryptographic weakness, mathematical distinguisher, collision, preimage,
   differential/linear anomaly, side-channel leak, or implementation defect
   discovered through testing or cryptanalysis should be disclosed responsibly
   and ethically to the project maintainers or published transparently in
   accordance with responsible disclosure standards.

4. EXPERIMENTAL STATUS & NO MISSION-CRITICAL WARRANTY:
   THE SOFTWARE IS EXPERIMENTAL AND CURRENTLY SUBJECT TO AN OPEN ACADEMIC
   CRYPTANALYSIS CHALLENGE. IT IS NOT CERTIFIED FOR MISSION-CRITICAL,
   LIFE-SAFETY, MILITARY, OR HIGH-VALUE PRODUCTION SYSTEMS WITHOUT INDEPENDENT
   AUDIT AND VALIDATION.

